-- **Commit identity is `DeepanshuOP` with the operator's GitHub noreply email.** Before any commit, verify with `git config user.name && git config user.email`. If either is wrong, **STOP and report** — GitHub attributes by email, and a mismatch drops the commit from the operator's contribution history. Repo-local config only; never touch `--global`.
+- **Commit identity is the operator's own identity, repo-local.** Whoever is running the session commits as themselves: `prishsha <prishavadhavkar@gmail.com>` for Prisha (Architect ruling, 2026-10-03), `DeepanshuOP` with his GitHub noreply email for Deepanshu. Before any commit, verify with `git config user.name && git config user.email`. If it is not the running operator's identity, **STOP and report** — GitHub attributes by email, and a mismatch drops the commit from that operator's contribution history. Repo-local config only; never touch `--global`.
 - **No trailers, ever.** Never append `Co-Authored-By`, `Claude-Session`, or anything else to a commit message. This history carries no trailers. Use the operator's `-m` string verbatim and nothing more.
